<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amanuban</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amanuban was a traditional <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atoni">Atoni</a> kingdom in the interior of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-timor">West Timor</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, centred on Niki Niki. Long recognised as one of the larger domains of the island, its rulers resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> control until the early 20th century. Its lands lie in the present South Central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timor">Timor</a> regency.</p></div>
